sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, R1-R4, single-swamp-node; DECISIONS scope (SQLite only when chosen, Schedules move, cert from destination CSR in-run), 1 (signing is the one step→Gateway call), 2 (DNS held); .env and Processes as in instance.create. docs/reference/instance-transfer.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:transfer
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane D icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant S as Node 12<br/>source · over ssh
  participant D as Node 15<br/>destination · ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:transfer 42 15<br/>--sqlite-source-path=… --force
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:transfer 42 15 --sqlite-source-path=/fast/apps/acme/feature/database/database.sqlite --force`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> <node> [--name=NAME] [--sqlite-source-path=PATH] [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - moves development Instance 42 from Node 12 to Node 15; the Instance id and Project stay
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--force`, the CLI asks for consent that names the source, destination and downtime; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--force` is required
  %%> Options:
  %%> - `--name`: another Instance name on Node 15
  %%> - `--sqlite-source-path`: also copy this SQLite file; without it, no database file moves
  Note over GW: Preflight, render .env<br/>Instance 42 · task #5133
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has access grants to Node 12 and Node 15
  %%> - both Nodes have the `app-dev` role and belong to active Clusters
  %%> - Project 7 may be placed on Node 15, and the destination path is free
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active development Instance with one active Route, and no removal runs
  %%> Plans:
  %%> - the Processes from Project 7's definitions for `development`, with Node 15's ports
  %%> - the Route on Node 15, and the Schedules' new target
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - from the stored environment of Instance 42, with Node 15 values such as `APP_URL`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Instance 42 marked transferring; task #5133 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Pause Schedule triggers<br/>workflow trigger removal
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the native Swamp schedule trigger of each Schedule of Instance 42
  %%> - there is no Node work here; Schedules install nothing on Nodes
  %%> Why:
  %%> - no fire runs against Node 12 during the move
  GW->>SW: Push .env to the vault<br/>vault: env-5133
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `.env` can hold secrets, which travel only through the vault
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads it with `vault.get`; no step asks the Gateway for it
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-transfer
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run of `operation-instance-transfer` on Swamp serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - both Nodes' addresses and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - paths, Process plan, Route plan, SQLite path when chosen
  %%> - secrets only as vault key names
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>D: Check the destination<br/>@swamp/ssh · path, ports free
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the destination path is free and the planned ports are unused
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - Node 12 keeps running until Node 15 is known to be ready
  SW->>S: Stop source Processes<br/>Instance 42 only
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the Processes of Instance 42 on Node 12; downtime starts here
  %%> Keeps:
  %%> - the Process units, for a restore if the move fails
  SW->>S: Archive the checkout<br/>git state, SQLite if chosen
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - packs the Git history, branch, origin, index, unstaged edits and untracked files
  %%> - adds the SQLite file only when `--sqlite-source-path` was given
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - `.env`; the Gateway rendered a new one for Node 15
  %%> Linked worktree:
  %%> - becomes an independent checkout on Node 15; the common repository on Node 12 stays unchanged
  SW->>D: Copy, extract archive<br/>via 209 scratch · sha256
  %%> How:
  %%> - copies the archive over `@swamp/ssh` through private scratch space on 209, and checks its hash
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - extracts it into the destination path, as Node 15's managed user
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - paths or links that escape the checkout
  %%> Cleanup:
  %%> - removes the scratch archives on all three Nodes
  SW->>D: Write .env<br/>vault.get env-5133
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered `.env` from the vault into the checkout, readable only by its owner
  SW->>D: Run Project setup steps<br/>@swamp/ssh · own timeout each
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the Project's setup steps, as in `instance:create`, so dependencies match Node 15
  %%> Typical steps:
  %%> - `composer install`, `vp install`, `php artisan migrate`
  SW->>D: Make a CSR<br/>key stays on Node 15
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates a private key and a certificate signing request for the Route's domain
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the private key never leaves the Node that serves the Route
  SW->>GW: Sign the CSR<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
  %%> Why a call to the Gateway:
  %%> - only the Gateway holds the Orbit CA key
  %%> - this is the one call a step may make to the Gateway (decision 1)
  GW-->>SW: signed certificate
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the certificate for the CSR, scoped to task #5133
  SW->>D: Publish the Route<br/>Caddy site, PHP pool, reload
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the certificate, the Caddy site and the PHP pool on Node 15
  %%> - reloads Caddy; no restart
  %%> Cutover:
  %%> - from here Node 15 serves Instance 42
  Note over SW: DNS publication held<br/>open: Nick decides
  %%> Open:
  %%> - DNS publication for Routes is on hold (`native-dns-takeover-held`)
  %%> - until Nick decides, the run changes no DNS record
  SW->>D: Create, start Processes<br/>Project definitions · development
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the Instance's Processes on Node 15 from Project 7's definitions for `development`, and starts them
  %%> - Processes recorded as stopped stay stopped
  SW->>D: Check the destination<br/>Vite listens, site answers
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the Processes run and the Route answers on Node 15
  alt destination checks pass
    SW->>S: Retire the source<br/>Processes, site, cert, checkout
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the Process units, Caddy site, PHP pool and certificate of Instance 42 on Node 12, and reloads Caddy
    %%> - deletes only the checkout whose identity the run captured
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - Node 15 stays authoritative; the leftovers on Node 12 are reported for repair
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record Node 15<br/>Instance, Processes, Route
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42, its Processes and its Route are recorded on Node 15, in one change
    %%> - task #5133 succeeds
    GW->>SW: Publish Schedule triggers<br/>workflow.trigger.set · Node 15
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - sets each Schedule's trigger again, now with Node 15 as its target
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Schedules have moved; their next fire runs on Node 15
  else a step fails before cutover
    SW->>S: Restore the source<br/>start Processes again
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts the Processes of Instance 42 on Node 12 again; the source is untouched otherwise
    SW->>D: Discard the destination<br/>only the proven checkout
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes what the run created on Node 15, and only that
    %%> If cleanup fails:
    %%> - the leftovers stay visible as a failure; nothing unproven is deleted
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep Node 12, mark failed<br/>triggers back · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 stays on Node 12, active again; task #5133 fails
    %%> - the Gateway sets the Schedule triggers again for Node 12
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
